# Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820, SM-T825): the partitions Android's own code in the
# recovery has to find, in Android's fstab format. Everything else is in
# recovery/root/system/etc/twrp.flags, in TWRP's format: one TWRP-format line
# here and Android's parser rejects the whole file.
#
# /misc: the bootloader message. Android writes "boot-recovery" there before
# restarting to recovery and the recovery clears it. Without this line it
# can't, and S-Boot keeps starting the recovery.

/dev/block/bootdevice/by-name/misc      /misc   emmc    defaults    defaults
